@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/v1

### Health check (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Login — the response's accessToken is reused by the requests below
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@websyner.co",
  "password": "admin12345"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### Current profile (permissions included)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refresh the access token (uses the httpOnly refresh cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token

### Change own password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "oldPassword": "admin12345",
  "newPassword": "admin12345"
}

### Forgot password — emails a reset link (logged to console if SMTP is unset)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@websyner.co"
}

### Reset password with the emailed token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@websyner.co",
  "token": "paste-token-from-email",
  "newPassword": "newpassword123"
}

### Logout — clears the refresh cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### --- Failure cases worth checking ---

### Wrong password → 401, generic message (no account enumeration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@websyner.co",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Invalid payload → 400 with errorSources from zod
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### No token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
